Week 3 job posting analysis of skills:

I chose posting #3 and #4 from the prior week list. Below is a list of the BIG skills listed in both of the selected job postings (both required and the 'nice to have' skills):

Post #3: Principle Quantitative analyst – upper-mid-level

Required:
-	Bachelor’s degree 
-	Experience/demonstrated skills in quantitative analysis
-	Working with large data sets
-	Team collaboration, able to work interdepartmentally 
-	Communication to technical and non-technical audience
-	Good understanding of equity markets and technical info

Nice to Have: 
-	Experience with data set tools
-	Masters or advanced degree
-	Experience writing SQL, Python

Post #4: Seach Quality analyst - mid-level

Required:
-	Bachelor’s degree
-	2 years experience with large data sets in business and planning
-	Communication and presentation skills for presenting data
-	Ability to test hypothesis and make informed decisions
-	Ability to take data and run meaningful statistics that lead to actionable results

Nice to have:
-	Experience with data tools used by company
-	Experience with management and people managing


--------------------------What stood out to me? ---------------------------

I was expecting the degree requirement, but what caught me by suprise was the amount of experence needed for the mid level postiions listed. The average time was about 2-4 years for the position required when my expectation was 5+ years. Another thing that stood out was the communication AND presentation requirements. Presentation of data to not only to technical audiences but to non-technical as well. There was not as much of an emphasis on the technical skills in the postings, more tailored to the soft skills.
